You finally reach the underbrush. It's not as hot here compared to the open country, and the sickly sweet smell that was making you giddy is fainter now. This is quite timely, as the floral fragrance was already starting to make you dizzy. You fix your eyes on the objective, moving along the edge of the forest. It looks like it's just a stone's throw to the lake; in fact, it takes much longer before you step onto its oozy shore.